{% comment %}
  ============================================================
  Google Address Autocomplete — Tapandrate
  ============================================================

  Install:
    1. Online Store → Themes → (the LIVE theme) → ⋯ → Edit code
    2. Assets → Add a new asset → upload address-autocomplete.js
    3. Assets → Add a new asset → upload address-autocomplete.css
    4. Snippets → Add a new snippet → name it "address-autocomplete"
       → paste this whole file in
    5. Layout → theme.liquid → paste this line just before </body>:

         {% raw %}{% render 'address-autocomplete' %}{% endraw %}

  There is NO Google API key in this file, and there must never be one.
  Anything rendered by Liquid ends up in the page source where any visitor can
  read it. The key lives on the Tapandrate server; this snippet only knows the
  address of the lookup endpoint, which is safe to publish because that endpoint
  only answers approved storefront domains.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%} ---- Settings: edit these two lines only ---- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign lookup_endpoint = 'https://www.tapandrateai.co.uk' -%}
{%- assign restrict_to_country = 'GB' -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Characters typed before we ask Google. Raising this to 4 or 5 cuts the
  Google bill on a busy store.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign minimum_characters = 3 -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Optional. CSS selectors for address-line-1 inputs on custom forms, separated
  by newlines. Standard Shopify address fields are detected automatically, so
  most stores can leave this empty.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture extra_selectors -%}{%- endcapture -%}

<script>
  window.TapAndRateAddressAutocomplete = {
    proxyUrl: {{ lookup_endpoint | strip | json }},
    country: {{ restrict_to_country | strip | downcase | json }},
    selectors: {{ extra_selectors | strip | json }},
    minChars: {{ minimum_characters }},
    debug: false
  };
</script>

<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'address-autocomplete.css' | asset_url }}">
<script src="{{ 'address-autocomplete.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
